---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How this static website handles data, hosting, and contact."
>
  <article class="reading">
    <div class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">SITE NOTES</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Garage Sidequests is a static website. It has no user accounts,
        comments, contact forms, advertising scripts, or analytics configured in
        V1.
      </p>
      <h2>On your device</h2>
      <p>
        The site does not set cookies or use browser storage. Fonts and visual
        assets are served with the site, without third-party font services.
        External links do not load their destinations until you follow them.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The production deployment is intended for Cloudflare. Hosting providers
        process connection information, such as IP addresses and request
        details, to deliver and protect websites. Their infrastructure may
        retain operational or security logs according to their own policies and
        account settings. This site does not collect that information through a
        separate analytics service.
      </p>
      <h2>Email and external links</h2>
      <p>
        If you email the public contact address, your email provider and the
        receiving email service process your message. Your message and address
        are used to respond to your inquiry. Please don’t send sensitive
        information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Linked sites have their own privacy practices.{" "}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">
          Cloudflare’s privacy policy
        </a>{" "}
        describes its practices.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
      <p>
        This page will be updated if analytics or other data collection is
        introduced. Questions can be sent to{" "}
        <a href="mailto:hello@garagesidequests.com">
          hello@garagesidequests.com
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
